    <briefdescription>
<para>Thread-safe allocator adaptor. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Uses a spin lock on the assumption that contention here is extremely rare.</para>
<para>TODO: Using a spin lock on every allocation can be quite expensive when contention is high. Since this is mainly used for <ref refid="namespacellvm_1a8e612822d4ba7bb36c9c79582a567108" kindref="member">BumpPtrAllocator</ref> and <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_specific_bump_ptr_allocator" kindref="compound">SpecificBumpPtrAllocator</ref>, it&apos;d be better to have a specific thread-safe <ref refid="namespacellvm_1a8e612822d4ba7bb36c9c79582a567108" kindref="member">BumpPtrAllocator</ref> implementation that only use a fair lock when allocating a new slab but otherwise using atomic and be lock-free. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
